    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Translate to the Left or Top"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Just like you can move an element to the right or down using positive values, you can also use negative values to move it to the left or above."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Let's try this out. This time, we'll translate box 50px to the left and 100px above."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "html",
      "content": "1<h1>Translate 50px to the left and 100px above.</h1>\n2<p>Click the box to see the change.</p>\n3<div class=\"box\">Click Me!</div>"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "css",
      "content": "1.box:active {\n2    /* Moves box 50px to the left and 100px above */\n3    translate: -50px -100px;\n4}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Run the above code and click the box element to see how it moves 50px to the left and 100px above its original position."
    },
